course: dictionary
lesson: 11820
title: Biologist
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A biologist is a scientist who studies living things. That includes plants, animals, people and tiny living things like bacteria. When you meet this word, look for clues in the sentence. «The biologist looked at the pond water under a microscope and counted the tiny living things.» The words looked, microscope and living things tell you the biologist is studying life.
explain: Biologists observe, experiment and record. They watch closely, test ideas, and write down what they see. «Maya's class watched a biologist record how the seeds grew each week.» Writing down what happens each week is a clue that the biologist is careful and patient.
explain: Biologists can work in many places, such as hospitals, labs, zoos, oceans and forests. Some have special names that show their area. «A marine biologist studies fish and whales in the sea.» The word marine means to do with the sea, so a marine biologist studies sea life.
fact: A biologist is a scientist who studies living things.
fact: Living things include plants, animals, people and tiny living things like bacteria.
fact: Biologists observe, experiment and record how living things grow, feed, move and survive.
fact: A marine biologist studies sea life, and a wildlife biologist studies animals and plants in the wild.
fact: You can spot the word biologist by its clues: look for words like living things, microscope, or record.
exercise: «The biologist looked at a leaf under a microscope.» What does a biologist study? | Money and numbers | *Living things, such as plants and animals | Rocks and mountains | Stars and planets
exercise: Which kind of biologist studies sea life? | Dentist | Baker | *Marine biologist | Postman
exercise: «The biologist recorded how the seeds grew.» Find and copy the word that names the scientist. | *biologist | recorded | grew | seeds
test: «Biologists observe, experiment and record how living things grow, feed, move and survive.» Which place could a biologist work in? | A bakery | A shoe shop | A post office | *A zoo
test: What does the word biologist mean? | *A scientist who studies living things | A doctor who only treats teeth | A teacher of music | A person who makes maps of the sea
exam: Which sentence shows a biologist at work? | The artist painted a bright sunset. | The baker iced a big birthday cake. | The bus driver waited at the stop. | *The biologist counted the tiny bacteria under the microscope and wrote the results down.
